@startuml

start

:Power management subsystem architected as hard real-time task;
:Continuously monitor all voltage rails via PMIC and BMS within dedicated RTOS thread;

:Associated ISR triggered by hardware timer;
:Manage high-frequency sampling;
:Incoming telemetry debounced;
:Log to ring buffer protected by mutex;

if (Detect energy demand fluctuation?) then (yes)
  :Assess supply sufficiency;

  if (Deficit identified?) then (yes)
    :Initiate concurrent processes;

    fork
      :Employ polling loop with exponential backoff;
      :Check energy storage state-of-charge;
      if (State-of-charge < defined threshold?) then (yes)
        :Initiate controlled charging cycle;
      else (no)
      end if
    fork again
      :Verify availability of external energy source;
      if (Successful CRC-verified handshake?) then (yes)
        :Engage via CAN bus command;
      else (no)
      end if
    end fork

    :Re-evaluate energy allocation strategy;
    if (Optimization required?) then (yes)
      :Spawn parallel tasks to;
      fork
        :Dynamically adjust scheduling priorities within priority queue;
      fork again
        :Recalculate allocation ratios;
        :Meet guaranteed demands of critical loads;
      end fork
    else (no)
    end if

  else (no)
  end if
else (no)
end if

repeat
:Execute all recovery policies through staged verification cycles;
:Dedicated watchdog ensures system liveness;
repeat while(System converges to stable operating state) is(no)

stop

@enduml
